From 49aa33058dcbe9874f695b7c320ba84b1b03bc77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: baverrr <342259467+baverrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:32:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DocumentsUI: Use the RavenOS glass theme

Draw Files like the RavenOS glass Settings, always dark:

- Use raven_backdrop as the window background, with the file list,
  directory header and breadcrumb transparent over it. The strip pinned
  behind the toolbar stays solid so scrolling files don't show through.
- Turn the toolbar and search bar into a flat glass pill, and the
  selection bar into a solid surface pill.
- Draw grid items as glass cards with a hairline stroke and the theme's
  card radius, with no elevation; list rows are clear, and selected rows,
  roots and chips use the accent-tinted glass.
- Put the navigation drawer, menus, bottom sheets and dialogs on a solid
  surface (Android 11 has no backdrop blur), with the accent for the
  selected root, buttons and progress.

Every color comes from res/values/raven_glass.xml, so a product overlay
can recolor Files to match the device's Settings theme.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I0c3de533bcfe76e2a88fecea32cb1d005822970b
